---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Methodology"
  eyebrow="Transparent by design"
  lead="DeepGeno Watch automates collection and drafting, but reserves editorial authority for people. These boundaries explain what reaches the public catalog—and what does not."
  width="narrow"
>
  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2 id="workflow-title">Two gates, one public record</h2>
    <ol class="pipeline" aria-label="Publication workflow">
      <li><span>Monitor</span><p>Official APIs surface source records from preprint servers, bibliographic indexes, and selected journals.</p></li>
      <li><span>Normalize</span><p>Records are deduplicated, tagged, and ranked. A complete abstract is required before triage.</p></li>
      <li class="pipeline__gate"><span>Human gate 1</span><p>A curator chooses exactly one action: Summarize, Defer, or Dismiss. Candidate data stays private.</p></li>
      <li><span>Synthesize</span><p>The selected Paper becomes an Evidence Packet. A configured model produces a strict Draft Summary with claim-level evidence IDs.</p></li>
      <li class="pipeline__gate"><span>Human gate 2</span><p>One pull request per Paper exposes the Draft Summary, evidence depth, provider, model, and integrity metadata for review.</p></li>
      <li><span>Publish</span><p>Merging that pull request creates a canonical public record and triggers a fresh static build.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2 id="coverage-title">Coverage</h2>
    <p>
      The watchlist focuses on sequence-to-function models, DNA/RNA/protein language models,
      variant effect prediction, gene regulation and epigenomics, single-cell deep learning, and
      structural bioinformatics.
    </p>
    <dl class="source-grid">
      <div><dt>Preprints</dt><dd>bioRxiv and arXiv q-bio, cs.LG, and stat.ML</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Journals</dt><dd>Crossref metadata for a curated high-impact ISSN list</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Enrichment</dt><dd>Europe PMC open-access text and OpenAlex DOI metadata</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cadence</dt><dd>Daily discovery with overlapping windows and durable source checkpoints</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2 id="evidence-title">Evidence depth</h2>
    <p>
      Each Published Summary states the strongest material available when it was drafted. “Abstract
      only” means no accessible full text informed the synthesis. “Partial full text” means some
      body material was available. “Full text” means the main paper was available through a lawful
      source such as open-access JATS, HTML, or PDF.
    </p>
    <p>
      Claims carry compact evidence IDs that resolve to source URLs, document types, locators, and
      content digests. The site does not mirror publisher PDFs or figures. A digest verifies input
      identity; it does not independently validate a scientific claim.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="llm-title">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2 id="llm-title">How models are used</h2>
    <p>
      OpenAI and Anthropic are supported through separate structured-output adapters. The active
      provider and model must be explicitly configured, and there is no silent provider failover.
      Models synthesize an evidence packet into typed fields; they do not browse, call tools, or
      decide what gets published.
    </p>
    <ul class="guardrail-list">
      <li>Source text is treated as untrusted input.</li>
      <li>Generated output must pass the shared schema and evidence-reference checks.</li>
      <li>Generated strings are escaped and rendered as structured fields—never raw HTML or MDX.</li>
      <li>Provider, model, prompt version, schema version, input digest, and human approval remain public.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="meaning-title">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2 id="meaning-title">Editorial labels</h2>
    <div class="label-grid">
      <div><h3>Must-Read</h3><p>High expected value for the core research agenda.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Recommended</h3><p>Material contribution with broad or practical relevance.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Notable</h3><p>Worth tracking, even if narrower or more incremental.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Queued / Skimmed / Read</h3><p>Progress through the editorial reading workflow; not a quality score.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="scope-note">
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <p>
      DeepGeno Watch is a curated discovery aid, not peer review, clinical guidance, or a complete
      index of genomics research. Summaries may contain errors despite evidence checks and human
      review; follow the original paper before relying on a result.
    </p>
  </aside>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .method-section + .method-section {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .section-number {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 4vw, 2.55rem);
  }

  .method-section > p:not(.section-number) {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .pipeline {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: steps;
  }

  .pipeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(7.5rem, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    counter-increment: steps;
  }

  .pipeline li::before {
    display: none;
    content: counter(steps);
  }

  .pipeline span {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .pipeline p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .pipeline__gate {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-accent-soft), transparent 78%);
  }

  .source-grid,
  .label-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .source-grid div,
  .label-grid div {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .source-grid div:nth-child(odd),
  .label-grid div:nth-child(odd) {
    padding-right: 1rem;
  }

  .source-grid div:nth-child(even),
  .label-grid div:nth-child(even) {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  dt,
  .label-grid h3 {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  dd,
  .label-grid p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .guardrail-list {
    margin-top: 1.3rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .guardrail-list li {
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
  }

  .guardrail-list li + li {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .scope-note {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    padding: 1.4rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .scope-note h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .scope-note p {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .pipeline li,
    .source-grid,
    .label-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .pipeline li {
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }

    .source-grid div:nth-child(n),
    .label-grid div:nth-child(n) {
      padding-inline: 0;
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
